/-!
# Compact objects of `D_QCoh` of a quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic space

Let `X` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space over a scheme `S`. An object of
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is compact if and only if it is perfect. This is Stacks 09M8.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCompactObject_of_isPerfect_yoneda`: on a represented affine algebraic
  space, perfect objects are compact.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isAffineSpace`: on an affine algebraic space,
  perfect objects are compact relative to `D_QCoh`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQcohCompact_of_isPerfect` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCompactObject_of_isPerfect`: perfect objects are compact on a
  quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic space.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isCompactObject_iff_isPerfect`: Stacks 09M8.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isPerfect_generator`: Stacks 09IY, `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is generated by
  a single perfect object.

## Implementation notes

On a represented affine algebraic space `U = Spec R`, the derived sections `RΓ(E)` of a perfect
object `E` are perfect in `D(R)`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isPerfect_representedAffineDerivedSections_obj`), hence compact
(Stacks 07LT), and `E` is the image of `RΓ(E)` under the equivalence `D(R) ≌ D_QCoh(𝒪_U)`. An
affine algebraic space is isomorphic to a represented one, and compactness is carried back along
the derived pullback of that isomorphism, whose right adjoint commutes with direct sums. The
general case is the induction principle of Stacks 08GP, with the Mayer–Vietoris step
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isElementaryDistinguishedSquare`.

The source argues through the dual `K^∨` of Stacks 08JJ instead; the induction principle avoids
the internal Hom.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09M8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09M8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08GP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08GP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07LT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07LT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IY)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

attribute [-instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian
  Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesGrothendieck

attribute [local instance 5000] SheafOfModules.instAbelian

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

attribute [local instance 10000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- **Perfect objects of a represented affine algebraic space are compact in `D_QCoh`.** Their
derived sections are perfect, hence compact, objects of `D(R)` (Stacks 07LT), and `D(R)` is
equivalent to `D_QCoh(𝒪_U)` through the adjunction `Φ ⊣ RΓ`. -/
theorem isCompactObject_of_isPerfect_yoneda (U : BigFppfOver B S hS)
    [IsAffine ((BigFppfOver.toScheme B S hS).obj U)]
    (E : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS (yoneda.obj U)
      (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS U))
    (hE : (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS (yoneda.obj U) (isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS U)).IsPerfect
      E.obj) :
    IsCompactObject.{u} E := by
  let e := representedAffineDerivedEquivalence B S hS U
  have : e.inverse.Additive := Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products _
  have hM : IsCompactObject.{u} ((representedAffineDerivedSectionsQcoh B S hS U).obj E) :=
    (StacksDraft.Perfect.isPerfect_iff_isCompactObject _).1
      (isPerfect_representedAffineDerivedSections_obj B S hS U E.obj hE)
  exact (isCompactObject_iff_isCompactObject_obj e.inverse E).2
    (StacksDraft.Perfect.isCompactObject_of_iso_of_preadditive
      ((e.toAdjunction.rightAdjointUniq (representedAffineDerivedQcohAdjunction B S hS U)).app
        E).symm)

/-- The derived pullback along an identity morphism of algebraic spaces fixes every object. -/
def smallEtaleDerivedModulePullbackIdObjIso (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (E : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u} (ringedToposStructureRingSheaf B S hS X))) :
    (smallEtaleDerivedModulePullback B S hS (𝟙 X)).obj E ≅ E :=
  let K := DerivedCategory.Q.objPreimage E
  let eK : DerivedCategory.Q.obj K ≅ E := DerivedCategory.Q.objObjPreimageIso E
  (smallEtaleDerivedModulePullback B S hS (𝟙 X)).mapIso eK.symm ≪≫
    smallEtaleDerivedModulePullbackObjQIsoOfIsEtale (𝟙 X) (fun _ _ hφ => by simpa using hφ) K ≪≫
    DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso ((NatIso.mapHomologicalComplex (modulePullbackIdIso B S hS X)
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).app K ≪≫ (Functor.mapHomologicalComplexIdIso _ _).app K) ≪≫ eK

/-- **Perfect objects of an affine algebraic space are compact relative to `D_QCoh`.** The space
is isomorphic to a represented affine one; the derived pullback of a perfect object along the
inverse isomorphism is perfect, hence compact, and its derived pullback back along the
isomorphism is compact again (Stacks 08FB) and isomorphic to the object. -/
theorem perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isAffineSpace (W : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hW : IsAffineSpace B S hS W.1) : PerfectIsQcohCompact W := by
  intro E hE
  have hZ := B.contains_terminal
  obtain ⟨T₀, hT₀, ⟨i⟩⟩ := id hW
  let Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS := ⟨yoneda.obj T₀, isAlgebraicSpace_yoneda B S hS T₀⟩
  let e : W ≅ Y := ObjectProperty.isoMk _ i
  let E' : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS W.1 W.2 :=
    ⟨E, qcohDerived_of_isPerfect_derivedCategoryB W E hE⟩
  have hgE : IsCompactObject.{u} ((quasicoherentDerivedModulePullback e.inv).obj E') :=
    isCompactObject_of_isPerfect_yoneda T₀ _
      (isPerfect_smallEtaleDerivedModulePullback e.inv E hE)
  have hfqc : IsQuasiCompact B S hS e.hom.hom :=
    isQuasiCompact_of_isQuasiCompactSpace B S hS hZ Y.2
      (isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_of_isAffineSpace B S hS hZ (isAffineSpace_yoneda B S hS T₀ hT₀))
      (IsAffineSpace.isQuasiCompactSpace hW) e.hom.hom
  have hfqs : IsQuasiSeparated B S hS e.hom.hom :=
    isQuasiSeparated_of_isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_source B S hS hZ W.2
      (isAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated_of_isAffineSpace B S hS hZ hW) e.hom.hom
  exact (isQcohCompact_of_isCompactObject B S hS W _
    (isCompactObject_quasicoherentDerivedModulePullback e.hom hfqc hfqs _ hgE)).of_iso
    ((smallEtaleDerivedModulePullbackCompIso B S hS e.hom e.inv).app E ≪≫
      (smallEtaleDerivedModulePullbackCongr B S hS e.hom_inv_id).app E ≪≫
      smallEtaleDerivedModulePullbackIdObjIso W E)

attribute [-instance] CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.instHasPushoutsType in
/-- **Perfect objects are compact relative to `D_QCoh`** on a quasi-compact quasi-separated
algebraic space: the induction principle of Stacks 08GP, from the affine case
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isAffineSpace` and the Mayer–Vietoris step
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isElementaryDistinguishedSquare`. -/
theorem isQcohCompact_of_isPerfect (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS B.contains_terminal X.1) :
    PerfectIsQcohCompact X :=
  qcqs_induction_on_self B S hS B.contains_terminal X hqc hqs
    (fun Z _ => ∀ hZ' : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS Z, PerfectIsQcohCompact ⟨Z, hZ'⟩)
    (fun _ hV _ => perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isAffineSpace _ hV)
    (fun _ _ _ _ _ hsq _ _ _ _ hPU hPV hPP _ =>
      perfectIsQcohCompact_of_isElementaryDistinguishedSquare hsq (hPU _) (hPV _) (hPP _))
    X.2

/-- **Perfect objects are compact in `D_QCoh`** of a quasi-compact quasi-separated algebraic
space. -/
theorem isCompactObject_of_isPerfect (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS B.contains_terminal X.1)
    (E : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)
    (hE : (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect E.obj) :
    IsCompactObject.{u} E :=
  isCompactObject_of_isQcohCompact B S hS X E (isQcohCompact_of_isPerfect X hqc hqs E.obj hE)

/-- **Stacks 09M8.** Let `X` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space over `S`. An
object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is compact if and only if it is perfect. -/
@[stacks 09M8]
theorem isCompactObject_iff_isPerfect (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS B.contains_terminal X.1)
    (E : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2) :
    IsCompactObject.{u} E ↔ (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect E.obj :=
  ⟨isPerfect_of_isCompactObject X hqs E, isCompactObject_of_isPerfect X hqc hqs E⟩

/-- **Stacks 09IY.** Let `X` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated algebraic space over `S`.
There is a perfect object `P` of `D(𝒪_X)` such that an object `E` of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is zero if and
only if `Hom(P[n], E) = 0` for all `n ∈ ℤ`.

The compact weak generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_isCompactObject_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_of_qcqs` is perfect by
Stacks 09M8. -/
@[stacks 09IY]
theorem exists_isPerfect_generator (X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)
    (hqc : IsQuasiCompactSpace B S hS X.1)
    (hqs : IsAbsolutelyQuasiSeparated B S hS B.contains_terminal X.1) :
    ∃ P : DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2),
      (smallEtaleRingedSite B S hS X.1 X.2).IsPerfect P ∧
        ∀ E : QuasicoherentDerivedCategory.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2,
          IsZero E.obj ↔ ∀ n : ℤ, Subsingleton (P⟦n⟧ ⟶ E.obj) := by
  obtain ⟨G, hGc, hG⟩ := exists_isCompactObject_isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_of_qcqs B S hS
    B.contains_terminal X hqc hqs
  refine ⟨G.obj, isPerfect_of_isCompactObject X hqs G hGc, fun E => ⟨fun hE n =>
    ⟨fun a b => hE.eq_of_tgt a b⟩, fun hE => ?_⟩⟩
  by_contra hne
  have hne' : ¬ IsZero E := fun h => hne ((ObjectProperty.ι _).map_isZero h)
  obtain ⟨G', hG', n, f, hf⟩ := (ObjectProperty.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_iff _).1 hG E hne'
  rw [ObjectProperty.singleton_iff] at hG'
  subst hG'
  let ι := ObjectProperty.ι (QcohDerived B S hS X)
  let g : G.obj ⟶ E.obj⟦n⟧ := ι.map f ≫ (ι.commShiftIso n).hom.app E
  have hg : (shiftFunctor _ (-n)).map g ≫
      (shiftFunctorCompIsoId (DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)) n (-n)
        (add_neg_cancel n)).hom.app E.obj = 0 := (hE (-n)).elim _ _
  have hg0 : g = 0 := by
    apply (shiftFunctor (DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2)) (-n)).map_injective
    rw [← cancel_mono ((shiftFunctorCompIsoId (DerivedCategory (Modules.{u, u} B S hS X.1 X.2))
      n (-n) (add_neg_cancel n)).hom.app E.obj), hg, Functor.map_zero, zero_comp]
  apply hf
  apply ι.map_injective
  rw [← cancel_mono ((ι.commShiftIso n).hom.app E), Functor.map_zero, zero_comp]
  exact hg0

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
